From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HarnessOS <patches@harnessos.invalid>
Date: Sat, 1 Jan 2000 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: show per account status bar meters

The bar's density comes from upstream's measured levels (status-bar-density.ts):
compact, tightest-only, then a "+N" overflow chip. The per-account lanes render as
upstream's usage chips keyed by lane, so collapsing and the overflow name a lane,
never a provider. Upstream's Cursor headline and its ZCode provider are kept; the
weekly-first summary stays for every other provider, and ZCode's compact row names
its tighter pool as upstream's test fixes. cursorUsageMenu and the uninstaller test
upstream retired are upstream's now. On v1.4.222 a segment also shows a provider's
overage balance once a window is capped (upstream #25408); the account mark, that
balance and the retained-sample warning render side by side.

A failing lane stays marked at every density, also while its retry is in flight. Compact
drops its status label, so its warning mark names the reason on hover; a lane showing a
retained sample names it the same way; a "+N" chip that hides a failing lane takes the
warning tone and names the reason; the narrowest letter badge names it on its amber dot.
The lane marks live in usage-lane-marks.tsx, which keeps the segment file under
upstream's max-lines budget. The French e2e roster keeps the default right-side segments,
which main's UI sync restores anyway, so the bar it measures no longer changes mid-
assertion: at 1568px it is compact, and at 2560px the label is bounded.

Carried-Because: Preserve the deployed Orca fork concern on v1.4.222.
Tests: Declared unit and integration gates in components/orca/build.toml.

